--- 26.08.2024 ---

ok, so, decision was made to go with yocto and zephyr. Some nice people have ported yocto to duos and it builds. 
My next steps are:
	HW:
		- go through the whole project once more. 
		- add temp sensors
		- start figuring out the pinout
		- order the boards a couple of days before returning to zagreb
		- bringup
	SW:
		- checkout existing yocto projects and how they are configured, figured what are layers, distros, recipes etc
		- get zephyros working
		- get openamp working communication working
		- get serial on mcu working (device tree on both sides configured properly)
		- get systemd working
		- get ocpp python working, and other python packages
		- start implementing the code

	CLOUD:
		- get the FOSS ocpp implementation working (OPTIONAL)
		- integrate device and cloud

