--- 15.08.2024 ---
	hm, hm, what will I do with the architecture 

	these are the options
	mmu processor:
		- buildroot 
			- "official" build, more people working on it
			- already has support for all three platforms
			- manual adding of new packages
			- not sure what would be needed to move for example from one service daemon to another
			- 
		- yocto
			- recepies available 
			- not "official" 
			- need to add support for duos and duo256m
			- have some experience here
			- kas seems helpfull 
		-X nixos 
			- nice in concept, but I do not have enough experience with nix
		-X debian 
			- nice in concept as I have a lot of experience with debian, but every thing is unsupported
		-X something else - NO

	rtos processor:
		- FreeRTOS 
			- simple to make 
			- have experience with it
			- there are examples with it

		- ZephyrOS
			- minimal experience with it and a pretty steep learning curve
			- would be great to learn it as it actually is an OS and has a lot of devices and code available
			- there are some examples with it, and there is an PR for support that is in progress. 
			- has openamp support out of the box

Seems to me that there are two possible combinations, buildroot and FreeRTOS or yocto and ZephyrOS. I will first start with ZephyrOS and Yocto, and if I run into a wall, I will back onto buildroot and FreeRTOS as it seems more flat and direct. 

